<title>INDIA: India approves Mangalore refinery plan.</title>
<headline>India approves Mangalore refinery plan.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian cabinet on Friday approved a 35 billion rupee expansion of Mangalore Refinery and Petrochemicals Ltd, increasing annual output to nine million tonnes from three million.  </p>
<p>A government statement said the expansion was to be completed in 33 months.</p>
<p>MRPL is jointly owned by the Aditya Birla group of companies and state-run Hindustan Petroleum Corp Ltd.</p>
<p>Its refinery presently processes up to three million tonnes of crude per year.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
